{"name":"Grass Valley","hex":"#f4f7ee","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Grass Valley","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A city in Nevada County, California, United States.","A census-designated place in Pershing County, Nevada, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Grass_Valley"}],"entries":[{"title":"Grass valley","blocks":[{"text":"A grass valley is a meadow located within a forested and relatively small drainage basin such as a headwater. Grass valleys are common in North America, where they are created and maintained principally by the work of beavers or browser feeders. Rarely, they are associated with cienegas."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grass_valley","wikidata":"Q5597497"},{"title":"Grass Valley, Western Australia","blocks":[{"text":"Grass Valley is a small townsite 13 kilometres (8 mi) east of Northam, Western Australia in the Avon Valley area."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Grass_Valley_gnangarra-04.jpg/330px-Grass_Valley_gnangarra-04.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grass_Valley%2C_Western_Australia","wikidata":"Q5597469"},{"title":"Grass Valley (company)","blocks":[{"text":"Grass Valley is a manufacturer of television production and broadcasting equipment. Headquartered in Montreal, Quebec, it was formed by the March 2014 merger of the original Grass Valley with Miranda Technologies, which were both acquired by American networking company Belden in 2014 and 2012, respectively. In February 2018, owners Belden merged Grass Valley with newly acquired Snell Advanced Media. On July 2, 2020, Grass Valley announced the completion of its acquisition by private equity firm Black Dragon Capital from Belden Inc."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grass_Valley_(company)","wikidata":"Q1475272"},{"title":"Grass","blocks":[{"text":"Grass refers to various families of plants. The three major families of grasslike plants are true grasses (Poaceae), sedges (Cyperaceae), and rushes (Juncaceae). Lawns and pasturelands are typically composed of true grasses, five of which cover 46% of the world's arable land: rice, wheat, maize, barley, and sugar cane."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Poa_annua.jpg/330px-Poa_annua.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grass","wikidata":"Q643352"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Grass_Valley_Post_Office_gnangarra-07.jpg/500px-Grass_Valley_Post_Office_gnangarra-07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Grass_Valley_Post_Office_gnangarra-07.jpg/1280px-Grass_Valley_Post_Office_gnangarra-07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Grass_Valley_Post_Office_gnangarra-07.jpg/500px-Grass_Valley_Post_Office_gnangarra-07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Grass Valley post office in 2024","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGrass_Valley_Post_Office_gnangarra-07.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/2009_Emir_of_Qatar_Cup_Final_-_DSC_0302_%283580952891%29.jpg/500px-2009_Emir_of_Qatar_Cup_Final_-_DSC_0302_%283580952891%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/2009_Emir_of_Qatar_Cup_Final_-_DSC_0302_%283580952891%29.jpg/1280px-2009_Emir_of_Qatar_Cup_Final_-_DSC_0302_%283580952891%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/2009_Emir_of_Qatar_Cup_Final_-_DSC_0302_%283580952891%29.jpg/500